-- Baseline marker migration — snapshot-chain repair (2026-09-01).
--
-- Context: this repo's migration snapshot chain (src/db/migrations/meta/*_snapshot.json)
-- was missing snapshots 0002 through 0035 (pre-existing gap, unrelated to any single
-- feature; not caused by this change). Because of that gap, `drizzle-kit generate`
-- could not compute a correct incremental diff — every invocation tried to recreate
-- the entire 72-table schema from scratch, which is exactly what produced this file's
-- original (auto-generated) content: full CREATE TABLE statements for every table
-- plus a spurious `ALTER TYPE ... ADD VALUE` for an enum value that was ALREADY
-- present in production (verified directly against the live DB before touching this
-- file — see the accompanying report).
--
-- Every one of those 72 tables, and every column, already existed in production
-- before this migration was generated (verified column-by-column against
-- information_schema.columns on the live `production` branch). Running the original
-- auto-generated DDL would therefore have failed outright (tables already exist) or,
-- worse, been destructive if anyone had "fixed" it into a DROP+CREATE.
--
-- This file is deliberately a NO-OP. Its purpose is not to change the database —
-- it never should be executed — but to give meta/0036_snapshot.json (generated in
-- the same `drizzle-kit generate` run, from the real schema.ts) a slot in
-- meta/_journal.json, so that `drizzle-kit generate` has a correct, complete
-- baseline to diff against for every future schema change. Historical files
-- 0000-0035 are untouched.
--
-- One real, pre-existing, UNRELATED drift was found while verifying this baseline
-- and is deliberately NOT fixed here (out of scope — see the report):
--   `ad_bookings.status` is `varchar(32)` in schema.ts but `varchar(24)` in the live
--   production DB. `drizzle-kit generate` will keep proposing an ALTER TABLE to widen
--   it until someone explicitly decides which side is correct and applies that fix
--   as its own reviewed change.
--
-- Do not edit this file to add real DDL. If schema.ts changes going forward, run
-- `drizzle-kit generate` again — it will now produce a normal, minimal, correct diff.
SELECT 1;
